course: dictionary
lesson: 13084
title: Figuratively speaking
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Most words mean exactly what they say. This is the literal meaning. Sometimes a writer uses a picture in words to make a point, and then the words mean something more than the plain facts. Figuratively means in a figurative way, not word for word.
explain: «Figuratively speaking, Maya is a lion on the pitch.» Maya is not really a lion. She has no mane and no tail. The picture tells you she is very brave and fierce, like a lion. Ask yourself: is this a real fact, or a picture?
explain: Figuratively is the opposite of literally. Literally means the plain, real meaning. «The tree literally touched the sky» could not be true. «The tree figuratively touched the sky» is a picture that says the tree is very tall.
fact: Figuratively means in a figurative way, not with the plain word-for-word meaning.
fact: Figuratively is the opposite of literally.
fact: «Figuratively speaking» tells the reader that the writer is using a picture, not stating a fact.
fact: «Figuratively, he is a lion» means he is brave.
fact: A good check is to try the plain meaning: if it makes no sense, the words are probably figurative.
exercise: «Figuratively speaking, Maya is a lion on the pitch.» What does figuratively show here? | *She is very brave, like a lion in a picture | She plays football with a lion | She is a real lion | She likes visiting zoos
exercise: Ben says, «My brother is figuratively a rock when I cry.» What does he mean? | He is made of stone | He lives near the sea | He is very heavy to carry | *He is a strong comfort to me, like a rock
exercise: Which word means the plain, word-for-word meaning? | *literally | lion | figuratively | pitch
test: «The tree figuratively touched the sky.» What does this picture tell us? | The tree was made of glass | The tree fell down in the wind | The tree was really touching the clouds | *The tree was very tall
test: Ava says, «Figuratively speaking, the classroom was a zoo.» What does she mean? | Animals were living in the classroom | *The classroom was very noisy and busy | The children were all asleep | The teacher had a pet snake
exam: Ruby asks, «What does figuratively mean?» Which answer is right? | A type of animal | Word for word, with the plain meaning | The same as literally | *In a figurative way, not the plain word-for-word meaning
